# Project Info

## Overview
A simple calculator web application served via a vanilla Node.js HTTP server (no frameworks/dependencies).

## Architecture
- `server.js` — Static file server using Node.js `http` module, serves files from `public/`. Runs on port 3001.
- `public/` — Frontend assets (HTML, CSS, JS). Pure vanilla JS with no build step or bundler.
- Calculator logic lives entirely in `public/script.js` as a single IIFE — no modules or external libraries.

## Key Details
- No `node_modules` or external dependencies — the project is entirely self-contained.
- The frontend uses `data-action` / `data-value` attributes on buttons with a single delegated event listener on `.buttons`.
- Keyboard input is also supported (digits, operators, Enter, Escape, Backspace).
